# BeELISA Release Notes

## 1.0.5 (03 Mar 2026)

### Added
- Data type recognition for pattern analysis
- loading Session from saved session loads as well saved analysis configs
- Logarithmic axis options for standard curve visualization
- Extended pattern plot statistics on X-Axis: IQR, mean, SD, median, and confidence intervals
- Plate grouping per user configuration

### Fix
- PCA handling for single plate groups (< 3 plates)


## 1.0.4 (28 Feb 2026)

### Added
- Inter-plate correction integrated into standard curve
- Optional blank subtraction with automatic negative control fallback
- Logarithmic axis options for standard curve visualization
- Extended pattern plot statistics: IQR, mean, SD, median, and confidence intervals
- PCA handling for single plate groups (< 3 plates)


## 1.0.3 (25 Feb 2026)

### Fix
- Windows: Both SplitContainer panels scroll
- Linux: Both panels scroll and Scrollcontainers are not None
- macOS: App loads past splash; both panels scroll after deferred assign
- all platforms running


## 1.0.2 (24 Feb 2026)

### Fix
- Crossplatform ScrollContainer not None in GTK & Cocoa object construction


## 1.0.1 (24 Feb 2026)

### Added
- macOS build (Apple Silicon ARM64)
- macOS build (Intel x86_64)
- Linux Flatpak package for native Linux distribution

### Changed
- Improved multi-platform CI/CD workflow via GitHub Actions
- Minor packaging and stability refinements


## 1.0.0 (22 Feb 2026)

### Release
- First stable release of BeELISA
- Packaged and deployed for Windows (MSI installer)
- Feature set finalized for Bachelor thesis submission